From ba1f3d631e115cb996e04a492fae2e1904b1b809 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <phlink@local>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 21:39:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 9 plan 09-02 BundleWriter codec
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds chrome/browser/phlink/portability/bundle_writer.{h,cc} — the codec
half of the .phlinkbundle export pipeline:

- POSIX ustar archive (forward-slash UTF-8, deterministic mtime=0).
- Synthesizes MANIFEST.json as the first tar entry (sha256 per entry).
- zstd-compresses the tar (level 3).
- AEAD-seals via phlink_crypto with the 69-byte header bound as AAD.
- 16-byte salt, 24-byte nonce sourced from boringssl RAND_bytes.

Unit tests cover header-shape, full round-trip
(write -> AeadOpen -> ZSTD_decompress -> verify ustar magic), and
wrong-passphrase rejection.

The export_service / mojom / settings WebUI bits enumerated in plan 09-02
are deferred to a follow-up sub-plan; this patch lands the
security-critical, format-defining piece in isolation so the on-disk
layout from docs/dev/profile-bundle-format.md is locked.
